<title>GREECE: SCHEDULE ON GREEK CORPORATE BRIEFINGS.</title>
<headline>SCHEDULE ON GREEK CORPORATE BRIEFINGS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corporate briefings of Greek institutional investors by Athens bourse listings continues with Yalco , the household goods retailer, metals trader Mytilineos and General Commerce , the power tools wholesaler, on Wednesday May 7, 1997.</p>
<p>The presentations are part of regular briefings over the fundamentals and business plans of listed Greek companies held on a weekly basis.</p>
<p>A total of 39 listed companies have come under the scrutiny of Greek institutional investors since Dec 18, 1996.</p>
<p>Around 30 more are slated for a presentation in the coming months.</p>
<p>The schedule for the coming weeks is as follows:</p>
<p>May 7, 1997  Yalco </p>
<p>		 Mytilineos </p>
<p>		 General Commerce </p>
<p>May 14, 1997 Viohalko </p>
<p>		 Hellenic Cables </p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301-3311812-4</p>
</text>
